1. TECHNOLOGY STACK AND REQUIRED LIBRARIES
==================================================

Use the following technologies and libraries.

| Requirement | Library |
|---|---|
| Frontend Framework | React.js + Vite |
| Programming Language | JavaScript (ES6+) |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS |
| Routing | React Router DOM |
| Icons | Lucide React |
| General Animations | Motion (motion/react) |
| Advanced Scroll Animations | GSAP + ScrollTrigger |
| Animated Illustrations | Lottie |
| Smooth Scrolling | Lenis |
| 3D Animations | React Three Fiber + Three.js |
| UI Components | shadcn/ui |
| SEO | React Helmet Async |
| Form Handling | React Hook Form |
| Form Validation | Zod |
| Notifications | Sonner |
| Carousel / Slider | Swiper.js |
| Utility Styling | clsx + tailwind-merge |

LIBRARY IMPLEMENTATION GUIDELINES:

A. Lucide React
- Use Lucide React consistently for icons.
- Use appropriate icons for navigation, academics, courses, facilities, admissions and contact information.
- Maintain consistent icon sizes and stroke widths.
- Avoid mixing different icon libraries.

B. Motion (motion/react)
- Use for general interface animations.
- Animate page transitions.
- Add subtle entrance animations to sections.
- Animate buttons, cards, dropdowns and navigation.
- Add smooth hover and tap interactions.

C. GSAP + ScrollTrigger
- Use for advanced scroll-based animations.
- Implement selected parallax effects.
- Use sophisticated image and text reveals.
- Create scroll-triggered section transitions where appropriate.
- Properly clean up animations and ScrollTriggers on component unmount.

D. Lottie
- Use for selected animated illustrations.
- Suitable for admission processes, student activities and educational highlights.
- Keep animations lightweight.
- Avoid excessive decorative animations.

E. Lenis
- Implement smooth page scrolling.
- Integrate correctly with GSAP ScrollTrigger.
- Ensure compatibility with anchor links and React Router.
- Respect reduced-motion preferences.
- Avoid conflicts with browser scrolling.

F. React Three Fiber + Three.js
- Use only when 3D adds meaningful visual value.
- Suitable for an optional 3D hero visual or subtle educational illustration.
- Lazy-load 3D components.
- Optimize performance.
- Provide static fallbacks for mobile and low-powered devices.
- Do not add unnecessary 3D effects to every page.

G. shadcn/ui
Use shadcn/ui for:
- Dropdown menus.
- Dialogs and modals.
- Accordions.
- Tabs.
- Select menus.
- Buttons.
- Form components.
- Tooltips.
- Navigation menus.
- Mobile navigation sheets.

Customize the components to match the Sambhram PU College design system.

ANIMATION RULES:
- Motion for regular UI animations.
- GSAP for advanced scroll animations.
- Lottie for standalone illustrations.
- React Three Fiber for selected 3D elements.
- Lenis for smooth scrolling.
- Do not use multiple animation libraries for the same animation.
- Avoid unnecessary animation complexity.
- Prioritize performance and accessibility.
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion.

